  <section|Status><label|status>

  Draft, awaiting independent mathematical and source review. Source pin:
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464> from
  <verbatim|source/upstream.json>.

  Owned prose: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/marked-portfolio-calibration.tex>.

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <subsection|Fixed section producer><label|fixed-section-producer>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.Push.Mark.Portfolio.build>, <verbatim|weaveBuild>,
    <verbatim|columns>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/RELAY_MARK/Portfolio.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|Imprint>, <verbatim|Campaign>, <verbatim|unsym>,
    <verbatim|regrade_tri>, <verbatim|twist>, <verbatim|cost_reel>,
    <verbatim|form_reel>, <verbatim|paid_reel>, <verbatim|reel_gauge>,
    <verbatim|reel_real>, <verbatim|reel_orient>, <verbatim|twist_real>,
    <verbatim|twist_orient>, <verbatim|twist_unit>, <verbatim|reel_unit>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/RELAY_MARK/Automorphism.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|powered>, <verbatim|powered_pose>, <verbatim|pose_power>,
    <verbatim|synchronize>, <verbatim|amalgamate>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/RELAY_MARK/Powered.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|SectionData>, <verbatim|SectionData.Sound>,
    <verbatim|SectionData.places>, <verbatim|SectionData.footprint>,
    <verbatim|SectionData.eval_linear>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/Source/Local.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|Work.G06.enclose>, <verbatim|Work.G06.realize>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/G06.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|Work.G07.answer>, <verbatim|paid_lumin>,
    <verbatim|Rate.mul>, <verbatim|Rate.lower_pay>, <verbatim|Rate.postcomp>,
    <verbatim|rate_link>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/G07.lean> and
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/G07/Stencil.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|Credit>, <verbatim|pop>, <verbatim|G06>, <verbatim|G07>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Source.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|commissioned>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/RELAY_MARK/Assembly.lean>.
  </itemize-minus>

  The current TeX result is conditional on an imprint. It identifies the
  actual filtration precisely: <verbatim|Powered> is generated by products of
  <verbatim|Chip = Slot \<times\> ColorIndex> coordinates, where each
  <verbatim|slotted> factor is one real color coordinate of a
  based/transported curvature slot. It is not raw link-entry degree.
  <verbatim|stamp (r,s)=(s,r)> is the lexicographic order used by
  <verbatim|Rising.lean>; <verbatim|stamp_monotone> is the exact implication
  that a stamp increase cannot reduce the slot count.

  For an imprint, the regrading inversion is finite triangular
  back-substitution on the grade components. <verbatim|cost_reel> puts the
  response of each basis element into <verbatim|powered> at its second grade.
  <verbatim|powered_pose> constructs a finite slot list and pose with the
  required lower total degree. <verbatim|G06.enclose/realize> supplies one
  common finite stencil and exact polynomial evaluation. Linear extension
  gives <verbatim|SectionData>; its <verbatim|Sound> fields follow from the
  imprint identities, the equation-ideal clause is the paid Micro conclusion,
  and <verbatim|pop> is the pose-list/stencil witness. <verbatim|G07.answer>
  obtains <verbatim|Credit> by <verbatim|paid_slot>, the product rule
  <verbatim|Rate.mul>, finite addition, and <verbatim|paid_lumin>. Its
  quantification is over the budget's Healthy translated stencil and
  admissible direction lists; no raw-link-degree assertion is made.
  <verbatim|commissioned> selects such data for every degree before later
  schedule choices.

  <verbatim|Linear.unsym> does produce the campaign in the formal route,
  using <verbatim|shelf>, <verbatim|marked_shelf>, and <verbatim|one_floor>;
  <verbatim|HGroup.impression> then averages over the signed group and
  conjugation. The prose gives the finite symmetrization argument but does
  not yet expand the analytic campaign producer (<verbatim|positioned> and
  its Taylor/ideal inputs). Thus the conditional section theorem is not being
  reported as an independent proof of that producer, nor as an unconditional
  result from <verbatim|Hol> alone.

  <subsection|Schedule purchase><label|schedule-purchase>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|paper>, <verbatim|oyster>, <verbatim|dusk>,
    <verbatim|shower>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Apres.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|puffs>, <verbatim|barunit>, <verbatim|pre_tilt>,
    <verbatim|collect_upper>, <verbatim|eventually_transitions>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Loan.lean> and <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/PRICE_COMPILER/Basic.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|sphere>, <verbatim|storms>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Matter.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|betaF>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/Pressure/Seeds.lean>.
  </itemize-minus>

  The prose expands the stagewise thresholds: for each fixed pair
  <verbatim|(d,i)> the portfolio supplies a finite credit, and
  <verbatim|L^(1/8)> eventually pays its fixed sphere cost. The maximum over
  the finite set <verbatim|d\<leq\>i> and door indices <verbatim|j\<leq\>i>
  supplies the one threshold for stage <verbatim|i>. For the delay, the
  source <verbatim|cash> inequality reduces to
  <verbatim|L^(d+1)*(x+b_L)^winter(d) \<leq\> (x+b_L)*x^winter(d)>; using
  <verbatim|0\<leq\>b_L\<leq\>x> it follows once
  <verbatim|x\<geq\>L^(d+1)*2^winter(d)>. <verbatim|eventually_transitions>
  collects the same and adjacent stage constraints, and
  <verbatim|collect_upper> forms their monotone prefix envelope while
  retaining the original delay.

  <subsection|Field calibration and public
  caller><label|field-calibration-and-public-caller>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|sliver>, <verbatim|chipcost>, <verbatim|cheaper>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Marimba.lean>. The source coefficient norm
    is the finite <verbatim|ell^1> norm. The exact estimate is
    <verbatim|\|\|Id-decor\|\|\<leq\>orbitCost^2*sliver=1/2>, followed by
    injectivity, finite-dimensional surjectivity, and inverse norm at most 2.

    <item><verbatim|Braze>, <verbatim|matter>, <verbatim|Hearth>,
    <verbatim|solaris>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Canopy.lean>. The exact
    producer input is the eventual triple: (i) a <verbatim|Credit> at each
    profile's order and power, (ii) <verbatim|0\<leq\>b_i\<leq\>hatBeta_i>,
    and (iii) the flight inequality <verbatim|2(1+columns_i)*sphere_i(b_i)\<leq\>puffs(block_{i-1})*sliver>.
    The selected solaris proof also consumes <verbatim|Parterre.inviting> and
    <verbatim|Figment.figment>; these are mathematical field/purchase
    estimates, not consequences of <verbatim|Portfolio.build> or the inverse
    lemma.

    <item><verbatim|inviting>, <verbatim|storms>, <verbatim|sanded>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Parterre.lean> and <verbatim|Matter.lean>.
    <verbatim|inviting> also requires the exact stencil containment, local
    forced-allowance/cover-number bound, positive allowance <verbatim|u_N>,
    nonnegative label budget <verbatim|\<zeta\>>, keeper, and forced-site
    spread estimate.

    <item><verbatim|figment>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Figment.lean>. It
    consumes the actual <verbatim|Cream> estimates, the cost/height/carol
    receipts, strict reference-depth margin, and source history conditions;
    it returns the re-centering correction and all earlier-scale motion
    bounds.

    <item><verbatim|potage>, <verbatim|catalog>, <verbatim|catalog_symm>,
    <verbatim|marshal>, <verbatim|Scotia>, <verbatim|reception>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Potage.lean>, <verbatim|Chaletbin.lean>,
    <verbatim|Eureka.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|Hearthside>, <verbatim|fireplace>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fire.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|hearthstone>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Hearth.lean>.
  </itemize-minus>

  The public caller consumes a common degree-indexed section/regrading in
  <verbatim|hearthstone>. For each fixed degree, its strict reference-depth
  margin makes the schedule stage index eventually large enough for that
  degree. The credit and flight clauses are exactly the matching
  <verbatim|paper> entries; <verbatim|shower> provides the adjacent delay
  inequalities, and the schedule recurrence turns the amount bound into the
  running allowance bound. These are assembled into the three
  <verbatim|Braze> clauses in the actual <verbatim|hearthstone> caller. The
  section enters <verbatim|solaris> with this history-produced
  <verbatim|Braze>, and <verbatim|fireplace> assembles the resulting
  <verbatim|Hearth> data with the finite equation-ideal catalogs and their
  symmetry receipts. The same portfolio currency is used by <verbatim|oyster>
  and passed in the schedule paper; the <verbatim|shower>-raised delays are
  consumed by the finite history. No alternative degree-dependent section is
  introduced after those purchases.

  <section|Exact open boundary><label|exact-open-boundary>

  This unit proves the conditional section/regrading/currency producer from
  an imprint, the elementary stage and delay threshold arithmetic, and the
  finite-dimensional small-error inverse estimate. The source does provide
  <verbatim|Linear.unsym> and <verbatim|HGroup.impression>, but the analytic
  proof that produces the initial campaign through <verbatim|shelf>,
  <verbatim|marked_shelf>, <verbatim|positioned>, and <verbatim|one_floor> is
  not expanded here; this is an upstream proof obligation. The public
  caller's assembly of the three eventual <verbatim|Braze> clauses uses the
  portfolio purchases as follows: <verbatim|oyster> supplies finite
  credit/sphere thresholds and <verbatim|pre_tilt> supplies the rate/barunit
  thresholds; <verbatim|shower> supplies the adjacent delay envelope; the
  strict reference margin makes each fixed degree eligible at sufficiently
  late stages. The fixed camera/Keeper and derivative fee come from the
  parent terminal-marked startup unit; the stencil containment/nonwrapping
  hypotheses come from centered-site geometry. They are inputs to, not
  conclusions of, this portfolio chapter. The separate marked-field producer
  obligations are:

  <\enumerate>
    <item>the local <verbatim|sanded> estimate
    <verbatim|sqrt(forcedAllowance_N)*storms(price(V_d),price(local_d))\<leq\>1>,
    together with the local invitation estimate after the already-supplied
    stencil, Keeper, and allowance conditions are inserted;

    <item>the finite-field <verbatim|Cream>/height/Carol budget chain needed
    by <verbatim|figment>;

    <item>the common-history attachment of those receipts to the chosen
    <verbatim|Hearthside> and catalog data.
  </enumerate>

  No such field estimate is inferred here from the unconditional existence of
  a portfolio section. Parent-owned terminal-marked startup/fixed-fee results
  are not repeated; this unit uses them only where cited by a future
  integration.

  <section|Checks><label|checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Inspected only the declarations and immediate dependencies listed
    above; no Lean command or build was run.

    <item>No TeX build was run.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was not run because
    the parent-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json> is absent
    in this clone.
  </itemize-minus>

